From 5938858ef971c8f64e875ac90b42d706f561230b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:50:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: baldur: Build the Qualcomm dwc3 glue in

defconfig has TYPEC=m. USB_DWC3_QCOM depends on TYPEC || TYPEC=n, so it
becomes a module before baldur.fragment sets TYPEC=y, and stays one.
Loaded late from the root file system, it holds back the pmic_glink
altmode driver, which waits for the controller as its mode switch.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment b/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment
index b1419efc0f..e5325b1153 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment
@@ -132,3 +132,7 @@ CONFIG_VIDEO_GC08A8=m
 CONFIG_VIDEO_DW9719=m
 CONFIG_LEDS_AW22127=m
 CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_PATTERN=y
+
+# The Qualcomm dwc3 glue depends on TYPEC || TYPEC=n. defconfig has TYPEC=m,
+# which makes it a module before this fragment sets TYPEC=y.
+CONFIG_USB_DWC3_QCOM=y
-- 
2.43.0

